#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""migood-sleepd: "Sleep & wake from anywhere" for Migood OS (runs as root).

The only part of the feature that needs root. The Migood Games app (signed in)
gets a wake ticket from the server (POST /api/remote/sleep) and hands it over
on the socket; from then on this service does the rest:

  sleep      set the RTC alarm for `every` minutes, suspend the PC
  check-in   the alarm wakes the PC: screen stays off, the person's apps are
             paused (frozen), Wi-Fi reconnects, and it asks the server
             POST /api/remote/wake/check {token}. Then, within 30 s of waking:
               wake:true        -> apps back, screen on, "Woken up from your phone"
               someone touched  -> apps back, screen on
               gone:true        -> stop sleeping (the ticket was forgotten)
               anything else    -> next alarm, back to sleep (apps stay paused)
  rescue     if this service stops or crashes mid check-in, apps are thawed and
             the screen turned on (ExecStopPost=... --rescue): a frozen desktop
             must never be what a person wakes up to.

Socket: /run/migood/sleepd.sock, one JSON object per line, one answer line each.
Only root and the Migood user of this PC may talk to it (checked with the
caller's real user id). Commands are only ever added, never changed:
  {"cmd":"status"}                         -> {"ok":true,"version":1,"sleeping":false,...}
  {"cmd":"sleep","token":"...","every":5}  -> {"ok":true}  (then the PC sleeps)
  {"cmd":"cancel"}                         -> {"ok":true}  (stop the sleep cycle)
  {"cmd":"resumed"}   root only, sent by the system-sleep hook after a resume

The ticket lives in /var/lib/migood-os/wake.json (root, 0600), never on a
command line or in the person's home.

  migood-sleepd            run the service
  migood-sleepd --dry-run  same, but "suspend" is a 10 s wait and no RTC alarm
                           is set: tests the whole check-in in a VM
  migood-sleepd --rescue   thaw the apps and turn the screen on, then exit
"""
